    "title": "<p>Immunohistochemical stains that aid in the distinction between thymic carcinoma and metastasis</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Anja C. Roden",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGridLight\" style=\"width: 715.1pt; border-collapse: collapse; border: none; \" border=\"0\" width=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid; height: 7.3pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 124.8pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 7.3pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"166\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong style=\"\">Immunohistochemical marker</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 590.3pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 7.3pt;\" colspan=\"3\" width=\"787\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center; page-break-after: avoid;\" align=\"center\"><strong style=\"\">% of cases expressing marker</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid; height: 3.5pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.35pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center; page-break-after: avoid;\" align=\"center\"><strong style=\"\">Thymic carcinoma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.7pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"180\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center; page-break-after: avoid;\" align=\"center\"><strong style=\"\">Non-thymic SCC</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 325.25pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"434\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center; page-break-after: avoid;\" align=\"center\"><strong style=\"\">Non-lymphoid metastasis other than SCC</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 124.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"166\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"\">CD5<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">20&ndash;100</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"180\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Lung: 0&ndash;15</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Skin: 0</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 325.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"434\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Lung adenocarcinoma: 9&ndash;26</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Prostatic adenocarcinoma: 22</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Ductal breast carcinoma: 27</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Pancreatic adenocarcinoma: 46</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Colon adenocarcinoma: 50</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Cholangiocarcinoma: 86</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 124.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"166\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"\">KIT (CD117)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">60&ndash;90</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.7pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"180\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Lung: 0<sup>b</sup>&ndash;20</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Oesophagus: 15</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Head and neck: 71</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 325.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"434\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Lung adenocarcinoma: 6&ndash;16</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Serous carcinoma: ~80</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Adenoid cystic carcinoma: up to 100</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Seminoma: up to 100</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 124.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"166\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"\">CD5 and KIT&nbsp;(CD117)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">65</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"180\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Lung: 0</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 325.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"434\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Lung adenocarcinoma: 4</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 124.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"166\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"\">PAX8</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Poly: 4&ndash;69</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Mono: 0</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.7pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"180\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Lung (poly): 0&ndash;2</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Lung (mono): 0</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Skin (poly): 0</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 325.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"434\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Lung adenocarcinoma (poly): 0&ndash;2</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">NSCLC (poly): 6</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Thyroid carcinoma (poly, mono): 80&ndash;100</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Clear cell RCC (poly): 95</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Breast carcinoma (poly): 0</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Gastrointestinal and pancreatic adenocarcinoma (poly): 0</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Endometrioid carcinoma (poly): 93</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Serous carcinoma (poly): 99</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 124.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"166\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"\">PAX8 (poly) and KIT&nbsp;(CD117)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">69</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"180\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Not reported</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 325.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"434\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">CK7+ chromophobe RCC with papillary architecture (mono): 87</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">NEC of the endometrium (poly): 4</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Thyroid <span style=\"\">CASTLE<sup>c</sup></span> (poly): 100 (1&nbsp;report)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">NSCLC: 0</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 124.8pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"166\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"\">PAX8 (poly) and CD5</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 130.35pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"174\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">49</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.7pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"180\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Not reported</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 325.25pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"434\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">NSCLC: 0</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CASTLE, carcinoma showing thymus-like elements; mono, monoclonal PAX8; NEC, neuroendocrine carcinoma; NSCLC, non-small cell lung carcinoma; poly, polyclonal PAX8; RCC, renal cell carcinoma; SCC, squamous cell carcinoma.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup><span style=\"\">a</span></sup><span style=\"\">Clones</span> 4C7, SP19, NCL-CD5&ndash;4C5. <sup><span style=\"\">b</span></sup><span style=\"\">Rarely</span> cytoplasmic. <sup><span style=\"\">c</span></sup><span style=\"\">Primary</span> or metastatic CASTLE might involve the upper mediastinum <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{26954328; 25899588; 19239992}</span>.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Table references: <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{31918172; 26945341; 26191237; 26643918; 24592933; 23958552; 30210064; 29975245; 29333007; 23801129; 16002927; 29970514; 12866374; 26898076; 15923166; 15086281; 21317881; 26076064; 16918976; 25596248}</span></p>",
